# Run notes (added after the run; everything below this block is the unedited transcript)
# - Where: a Mac mini (M4, macOS 15, arm64). The checkout was this branch, hard-reset to the commit
#   on the "repo" line, with a warm cargo target dir. That commit is the branch before its last
#   rebase onto main 5e3dac5, which added docs/CYCLES.md and the cycle tooling only: no change to
#   lezreg, the SDK, the program or this script's steps. It is a local commit, not on GitHub, so
#   the source pointers recorded in this run's entries name a commit nobody else can fetch.
# - No Docker and no node on that machine, hence the three SKIPs.
# - Sequencer: LEZ v0.4.0-rc3 (bafd07be) standalone. An earlier `scripts/demo.sh --prepare-only`
#   on the same machine built it from the tag (2063 s); this run took it from that cache.
# - Storage: the logos-storage v0.5.3 darwin-arm64 release, downloaded and sha256-checked by the script.
# - Environment specific to that machine:
#   - builds ran behind a shared build lock (DEMO_BUILD_WRAP), with CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4;
#   - r0vm was supplied through RISC0_SERVER_PATH (it is not on PATH there), with RISC0_DEV_MODE=1
#     and RAYON_NUM_THREADS=4. Nothing in this run proves: lezreg only executes (simulates)
#     public transactions.
# - The P1 row's "cycle_bench numbers are not done" predates docs/CYCLES.md and is superseded by
#   it; the script on the branch now points at docs/CYCLES.md there.
# - Run with --keep, so that `scripts/demo.sh --testnet` could then be exercised against the same
#   chain (docs/demo-testnet-mode.log).
